{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nMr. Chanek has an integer represented by a string $$$s$$$. Zero or more digits have been erased and are denoted by the character _. There are also zero or more digits marked by the character X, meaning they're the same digit.Mr. Chanek wants to count the number of possible integer $$$s$$$, where $$$s$$$ is divisible by $$$25$$$. Of course, $$$s$$$ must not contain any leading zero. He can replace the character _ with any digit. He can also replace the character X with any digit, but it must be the same for every character X.As a note, a leading zero is any 0 digit that comes before the first nonzero digit in a number string in positional notation. For example, 0025 has two leading zeroes. An exception is the integer zero, (0 has no leading zero, but 0000 has three leading zeroes).\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Java 8 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Solution {\n\n    public static Integer[][][] memo;\n\n    public static int countValid(int pos, int placeholderVal, int lastTwo, int n, String pattern) {\n        if (pos == n) {\n            return (lastTwo == 0 || lastTwo == 25 || lastTwo == 50 || lastTwo == 75) ? 1 : 0;\n        }\n        if (memo[pos][placeholderVal][lastTwo] != null) {\n            return memo[pos][placeholderVal][lastTwo];\n        }\n        int result = 0;\n        char c = pattern.charAt(pos);\n        if (c == 'X') {\n            if (placeholderVal != 10) {\n                result = countValid(pos + 1, placeholderVal, (lastTwo % 10) * 10 + placeholderVal, n, pattern);\n            } else {\n                for (int digit = (pos == 0 ? 1 : 0); digit < 10; digit++) {\n                    result += countValid(pos + 1, digit, (lastTwo % 10) * 10 + digit, n, pattern);\n                }\n            }\n        } else if (c == '_') {\n            for (int digit = (pos == 0 ? 1 : 0); digit < 10; digit++) {\n                result += countValid(pos + 1, placeholderVal, (lastTwo % 10) * 10 + digit, n, pattern);\n            }\n        } else {\n            int digit = c - '0';\n            result += countValid(pos + 1, placeholderVal, (lastTwo % 10) * 10 + digit, n, pattern);\n        }\n        return memo[pos][placeholderVal][lastTwo] = result;\n    }\n\n    public static void process(InputReader in, PrintWriter out) {\n        String s = in.next();\n        int len = s.length();\n        if (len == 1) {\n            out.println(s.equals(\"0\") ? 1 : 0);\n        } else if (s.charAt(0) == '0') {\n            out.println(0);\n        } else {\n            memo = new Integer[len][11][100];\n            out.println(countValid(0, 10, 0, len, s));\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        new Thread(() -> {\n            try (PrintWriter pw = new PrintWriter(System.out)) {\n                process(new InputReader(System.in), pw);\n            }\n        }).start();\n    }\n\n    static class InputReader {\n        private final BufferedReader br;\n        private StringTokenizer st;\n\n        public InputReader(InputStream is) {\n            br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(is), 32768);\n        }\n\n        public String next() {\n            while (st == null || !st.hasMoreTokens()) {\n                try {\n                    st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n                } catch (IOException e) {\n                    throw new RuntimeException(e);\n                }\n            }\n            return st.nextToken();\n        }\n\n        public int nextInt() {\n            return Integer.parseInt(next());\n        }\n\n        public long nextLong() {\n            return Long.parseLong(next());\n        }\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Solution {\n\n    public static Long[][][][] memo;\n    public static String pattern;\n    public static int n;\n\n    public static long countValid(int pos, int placeholderVal, int lastTwo, boolean started) {\n        if (pos == n) {\n            // Check if number is valid (has started, i.e., not all zeros) and divisible by 25\n            if (!started) return 0; // all zeros is invalid for numbers with length > 1\n            return (lastTwo == 0 || lastTwo == 25 || lastTwo == 50 || lastTwo == 75) ? 1 : 0;\n        }\n        \n        if (memo[pos][placeholderVal][lastTwo][started ? 1 : 0] != null) {\n            return memo[pos][placeholderVal][lastTwo][started ? 1 : 0];\n        }\n        \n        long result = 0;\n        char c = pattern.charAt(pos);\n        \n        if (c == 'X') {\n            if (placeholderVal != 10) {\n                // Fixed placeholder value\n                int newLastTwo = (lastTwo % 10) * 10 + placeholderVal;\n                boolean newStarted = started || (placeholderVal != 0);\n                // Handle leading zero case: if not started and placeholderVal is 0, still not started\n                if (!started && placeholderVal == 0) {\n                    newStarted = false;\n                }\n                result = countValid(pos + 1, placeholderVal, newLastTwo, newStarted);\n            } else {\n                // Need to try all possible values for X\n                for (int digit = 0; digit < 10; digit++) {\n                    // For the first digit, can't be 0\n                    if (pos == 0 && digit == 0) continue;\n                    \n                    int newLastTwo = (lastTwo % 10) * 10 + digit;\n                    boolean newStarted = true; // since digit != 0 when pos == 0, or started already\n                    if (pos > 0 && !started && digit == 0) {\n                        newStarted = false;\n                    } else {\n                        newStarted = true;\n                    }\n                    result += countValid(pos + 1, digit, newLastTwo, newStarted);\n                }\n            }\n        } else if (c == '_') {\n            for (int digit = 0; digit < 10; digit++) {\n                // For the first digit, can't be 0\n                if (pos == 0 && digit == 0) continue;\n                \n                int newLastTwo = (lastTwo % 10) * 10 + digit;\n                boolean newStarted = true;\n                if (pos > 0 && !started && digit == 0) {\n                    newStarted = false;\n                } else {\n                    newStarted = true;\n                }\n                result += countValid(pos + 1, placeholderVal, newLastTwo, newStarted);\n            }\n        } else {\n            int digit = c - '0';\n            // If this digit is 0 and we haven't started, still not started\n            boolean newStarted = started || (digit != 0);\n            if (!started && digit == 0) {\n                newStarted = false;\n            }\n            int newLastTwo = (lastTwo % 10) * 10 + digit;\n            result += countValid(pos + 1, placeholderVal, newLastTwo, newStarted);\n        }\n        \n        return memo[pos][placeholderVal][lastTwo][started ? 1 : 0] = result;\n    }\n\n    public static void process(InputReader in, PrintWriter out) {\n        String s = in.next();\n        pattern = s;\n        n = s.length();\n        \n        // Special case: single character\n        if (n == 1) {\n            if (s.equals(\"0\") || s.equals(\"_\") || s.equals(\"X\")) {\n                // For single digit, only 0 is divisible by 25\n                if (s.equals(\"0\")) {\n                    out.println(1);\n                } else if (s.equals(\"_\")) {\n                    out.println(1); // only 0 is valid\n                } else if (s.equals(\"X\")) {\n                    out.println(1); // only 0 is valid\n                } else {\n                    out.println(0);\n                }\n            } else {\n                out.println(0);\n            }\n            return;\n        }\n        \n        // Check if first character is '0' (invalid leading zero)\n        if (s.charAt(0) == '0') {\n            out.println(0);\n            return;\n        }\n        \n        // Initialize memo: [pos][placeholderVal][lastTwo][started]\n        memo = new Long[n][11][100][2];\n        long result = countValid(0, 10, 0, false);\n        out.println(result);\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        new Thread(() -> {\n            try (PrintWriter pw = new PrintWriter(System.out)) {\n                process(new InputReader(System.in), pw);\n            }\n        }).start();\n    }\n\n    static class InputReader {\n        private final BufferedReader br;\n        private StringTokenizer st;\n\n        public InputReader(InputStream is) {\n            br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(is), 32768);\n        }\n\n        public String next() {\n            while (st == null || !st.hasMoreTokens()) {\n                try {\n                    st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n                } catch (IOException e) {\n                    throw new RuntimeException(e);\n                }\n            }\n            return st.nextToken();\n        }\n\n        public int nextInt() {\n            return Integer.parseInt(next());\n        }\n\n        public long nextLong() {\n            return Long.parseLong(next());\n        }\n    }\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.5\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [0.0, -7.652943895664066e-05, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -8.999896090244874e-05, -1.1444026313256472e-05, -0.00043084874050691724, -4.0531076592742465e-06, -3.4570634852570947e-06, -4.792098479811102e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.00010871296399272978, -1.2278481335670222e-05, -0.00021109737281221896, -2.7179348762729205e-05, -1.8000440832111053e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.004218964371830225, -8.940656698541716e-06, -0.7519493103027344, -1.2278481335670222e-05, -0.17981666326522827, -0.0006599632324650884, -0.28117144107818604, -0.01251310296356678, -0.003038672497496009, -3.814689989667386e-06, -0.09182702004909515, -0.0565216988325119, -0.0620347298681736, -0.0003014348621945828, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -9.536738616588991e-07, -2.95634672511369e-05, -0.006839318200945854, -0.002186885569244623, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -0.00010084597306558862, -2.264974000354414e-06, -0.0018441352294757962, -0.00023326536756940186, -7.4741430580616e-05, -2.264974000354414e-06, -9.894321920000948e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.044312942773103714, -0.4467771649360657, -0.15430176258087158, -1.3828182090946939e-05, -0.20163288712501526, -0.02643745392560959, -4.8040190449682996e-05, -0.0001248043408850208, -0.14336353540420532, -0.3080953061580658, -0.3485247492790222, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -4.6491513785440475e-06, -1.6689160474925302e-05, 0.0, -9.536738616588991e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -0.7278087139129639, -0.361937016248703, -0.01670527085661888, -0.8269852